{
 "section_summary": "This section contains translated commercial messages intercepted at Chungking, together with embassy despatches transmitting them. The messages concern rice and packing bags, shipping shortages, trade controls, rubber barter, industrial supplies, insurance, and business reorganization across Japan, China, French Indochina, and Southeast Asia. It also includes a request for a speech by Joseph Grew and a diplomatic telegram reporting Japanese calls for severe reductions in civilian living standards.",
